<title>SOUTH AFRICA: CORNICK RAISES INTERIM LINKED UNIT PROFIT.</title>
<headline>CORNICK RAISES INTERIM LINKED UNIT PROFIT.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Feb 28 </p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Linked unit attrib (cts)    24.6  vs  19.7</p>
<p>    Debenture interest (cts)    16.8  vs  13.4</p>
<p>    Retained income		 1.38  vs  0.95</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			   2.12  vs  1.46</p>
<p>    Tax				 0.74  vs  0.51</p>
<p>    Interest paid		   1.11  vs  0.62</p>
<p>    Turnover			 54.70  vs 36.97</p>
<p>Full name: Pat Cornick Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The furniture company said that debenture interest</p>
<p>would be declared and paid by November 15.</p>
<p>It said the group's order book was at a sound level and the</p>
<p>directors are confident that the group's pattern at the turnover</p>
<p>level will be sustained. Continuing competition due to weakness</p>
<p>in demand may maintain short-term pressure on profit margins but</p>
<p>the group said it was well placed to counter these threats.</p>
<p>The directors believe that the fundamentals for growth in</p>
<p>the furniture market remain positive.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
